  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "Ba &lt; Ca &lt; Se &lt; S &lt; Ar<br /><br />Ba,&nbsp; Ca belong to gr IIA ( alkaline earth metals)<br /><br />Se and S belong to gr Vl A (Chalcogens)<br />and as we go down the group ionaization enthalpy decreases with increasing atomic size. So,<br />&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<br />&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;&nbsp; Ba &lt; Ca&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; and<br />&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;Se &lt; S<br /><br />Ar has stable completely filled electronic configuration and, therefore,has higest ionization enthalpy.Hence,the correct order is<br /><br /><math> <mrow> <mtable equalcolumns=\"true\" equalrows=\"true\"> <mtr> <mtd> <mrow></mrow> </mtd> <mtd> <mrow> <mtext>Ba</mtext></mrow> </mtd> <mtd> <mo>&lt;</mo> </mtd> <mtd> <mrow> <mtext>Ca</mtext></mrow> </mtd> <mtd> <mo>&lt;</mo> </mtd> <mtd> <mrow> <mtext>Se</mtext></mrow> </mtd> <mtd> <mo>&lt;</mo> </mtd> <mtd> <mtext>S</mtext> </mtd> <mtd> <mo>&lt;</mo> </mtd> <mtd> <mrow> <mtext>Ar</mtext></mrow> </mtd> </mtr> <mtr> <mtd> <mrow> <msup> <mrow> <mtext>in&nbsp;kJmol</mtext></mrow> <mrow> <mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow> </msup> </mrow> </mtd> <mtd> <mrow> <mn>503</mn></mrow> </mtd> <mtd> <mrow></mrow> </mtd> <mtd> <mrow> <mn>590</mn></mrow> </mtd> <mtd> <mrow></mrow> </mtd> <mtd> <mrow> <mn>941</mn></mrow> </mtd> <mtd> <mrow></mrow> </mtd> <mtd> <mrow> <mn>999</mn></mrow> </mtd> <mtd> <mrow></mrow> </mtd> <mtd> <mrow> <mn>1520</mn></mrow> </mtd> </mtr> </mtable></mrow> </math>",
